cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this bench, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mdaa_bench: simulation bench for blind identification of latent dynamical structure (MDAA)"
version: v7.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hudsonbonomo/mdaa_bench"
authors:
  - family-names: Bonomo
    given-names: Hudson A. R.
    affiliation: "TMU-LAB — The Machine Unconscious Lab, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0656-7641"
abstract: >-
  This version adds the fourth bench to the repository: the adaptive policy bench,
  supplementary material for Paper 6 (Adaptive Policy Learning in Situated Learning
  Accessibility).

  What is new. Five planted worlds (S, N, K, V, R) test whether a reader that adjusts
  a declared window under the rule of layer 6 separates from readers that each drop
  one rule of that paper. R_declared calls the @tmulab/mdaa plugin by subprocess with
  layer 6. R_fixed is the same plugin with a range of zero width, which is the window
  of Paper 5. R_simple drops replication, R_mix drops provenance, R_sym also shortens
  on contradiction, and R_cross counts across vocabulary regimes.

  Pre-registration and amendments. The pre-registration (adaptive/PREREGISTRO_v1.md)
  was frozen at commit bed380b, with SHA-256 hashes, line endings normalized to LF,
  verified by a guardian test (tests/test_adaptive_guardian.py). Three rounds of
  amendment (v0.3 to v0.5) were committed before the freeze, none from a result. A
  pilot on discarded seeds 901–905 (commit 65f5e6b) recorded only the control sides
  of the predictions and required no amendment.

  Grid. 400 runs (20 cells × 20 seeds), with the authorization and the results
  committed at 3cd0aad. Six of the eight pre-registered predictions are met. P1
  fails in one cell (S, T = 320, k = 5: 0.80 against a threshold of 0.90), which
  the pre-registration classifies as against the paper. P5 fails on its control
  side in one cell (K, T = 320, k = 3: R_sym 0.65 against 0.80), which it
  classifies as a defect of instrument. Results in
  adaptive/resultados/grid_adaptive_decision.json and grid_adaptive_rows.csv.

  Measured plugin. The grid ran against three compiled files of tmulab-mdaa at
  commit 04e71bb (dist/adjustment-cli.js, dist/adjustment.js, dist/standing.js),
  whose hashes are fixed in adaptive/plugin.sha256; the pilot and the grid refuse
  to run against any other build. The plugin repository is private. These three
  files and the source of layer 6 are deposited as supplementary material with
  Paper 6.
keywords:
